{================================================================================
 Script Name : _Backtest_Adaptive_Farmer_v14_PureLong
 MC Load Name: STRATEGY_WILLY_LONG_C_V151_RESEARCH
               *** DO NOT save over the live signal name
               STRATEGY_WILLY_LONG_C. Research build. ***
 Description : Matrix Range Capture (Full-Range Consolidation Long)
 Version     : v15.1 RESEARCH (v15.0 base + re-entry LABEL only, zero behaviour change)
 Symbol      : TXF1 (Taiwan Stock Index Futures Front Month)
 Platform    : MultiCharts 9.0 PowerLanguage x64
 Timeframe   : Data1 = 15M / Data2 = 60M / Data3 = Daily

 CHANGELOG v15.1 (2026-08-25) RESEARCH -- re-entry LABEL. No behaviour.

   WHY. L3 already re-enters. Today's bar-level research concluded it has a
   natural re-entry, must not be throttled -- any cooldown length costs
   19.8 to 28.7 pct of net and 95 pct of the loss comes from the Top-10 it
   destroys. What is missing is the LABEL: every entry ships as CL_Entry so
   a re-entry cannot be told apart in any report.

   WHY NOT THE L2 RECIPE. L2's definition ("previous trade lost AND this
   entry is at or below the previous entry price") does not transfer. On L3
   it selects 134 of 360 trades, 37 pct of everything. L3 enters at
   v_Box_Btm with a Buy Stop and the box bottom is a MOVING structural
   level, so "entry at or below the previous entry" mostly means "the box
   did not move up" -- not a re-entry at all. Requiring an exactly equal
   entry price collapses the other way, to a single trade, because the box
   bottom is a rolling Lowest and almost never repeats.

   THE DEFINITION USED, user ruling 2026-08-25 option A:

     the SAME consolidation episode, previous trade stopped out at a loss,
     and the new order price at or below the interrupted entry price.

   v_is_in_consolidation is sticky exactly as in L4: it turns true when the
   box qualifies and false only when the Data2 close leaves the box. An
   episode counter increments on each false->true transition, so "same
   episode" is a single integer comparison. Zero free parameters -- no time
   window, no tolerance band.

   And unlike L2, the comparison is sound at decision time: the order price
   IS v_Box_Btm, known when the order is placed. L2 v5.4 exposed the trap of
   comparing a fill price that does not exist yet; a Buy Stop has no such
   gap.

   PositionProfit(1) <= 0 for the loss test, same reasoning as L2 v5.4: it
   answers identically whether MC reports gross or net.

   v_MktExit_Ordered excludes market exits. L3 differs from L2 here -- 33 of
   its 200 losing exits are NOT stops (28 CL_BreakExit, 4 CL_Holiday, 1
   CL_Settlement), so "closed at a loss" alone would over-count. The flag is
   reset each bar in position and set at all five market-exit sites.

   NOT changed: the entry conditions, the exit chain, every input.

   ANCHOR: must reproduce v15.0 exactly -- 360 trades / 1,389,600.
   The only thing that may move is the split CL_Entry + CL_ReEntry = 360.

   Count cannot be pre-registered: "same episode" needs bar data, which the
   trade list does not carry. Registered as a RANGE instead --
   20 <= CL_ReEntry <= 115, expected near the low end. Above 115 means the
   episode gate is not working.

   Research record: docs/research/L3_reentry_barlevel_research_20260825.md

 ARCHITECTURE REDESIGN (v14.0, 2026-07-03):
   Problem: v13 half-box design splits the box into Bot->Mid and Mid->Top,
            structurally capping reward ratio at ~1.1x. CL_Entry_Bot was a
            dead leg (26 trades, -10.4K). 94% of profit came from
            CL_Entry_Mid targeting only half the box range.

   Solution: Multi-dimensional matrix architecture.
     Dim 1 [Box Qualification]: skip boxes < Min_Box_ATR * ATR (friction filter)
     Dim 2 [Support Zone]:     unified entry at bottom Entry_Zone_Pct of box
     Dim 3 [Dynamic Target]:   Frozen swing high (15M lookback, capped at Box_Top)
     Dim 4 [Trend + Daily]:    unchanged filters from v13

   Pre-verify: Python 28y TWII daily confirmed direction:
     Full-range PF 1.086 vs half-box PF 0.806 (+35%)
     Reward ratio 1.92x vs 0.90x (+113%)
     Filtered variant (large boxes) best: Sharpe +0.366 vs baseline

   Changes from v13.4:
     - REMOVED: CL_Entry_Bot / CL_Entry_Mid dual-leg split
     - REMOVED: v_Leg_IsBot / v_Work_IsBot leg classification
     - REMOVED: CL_TP_Bot / CL_TP_Mid dual-leg targets
     - ADDED:   CL_Entry (unified support zone entry)
     - ADDED:   CL_TP (full-range target = dynamic swing high)
     - ADDED:   Entry_Zone_Pct input (support zone = bottom 50% of box)
     - ADDED:   Min_Box_ATR input (box must be >= N * ATR to trade)
     - ADDED:   Swing_Lookback input (15M bars for dynamic target)
     - KEPT:    All safety modules (Holiday v3, Settlement, ImmediateStop,
                FrozenSL, BreakExit, Registry fail-safe, Manual Kill)
     - KEPT:    BE mechanism code (disabled, BE_Trigger_Pts=0)

 V15.0 CHANGES (2026-07-25, stop loss hardening):
   BUG-1 FIX: Added SetStopContract declaration.
     Without it, 2-lot deployment halves the per-contract stop distance.
     SetStopContract makes SetStopLoss amount per-CONTRACT (lot-invariant).
   BUG-2 FIX: Added SL_Pct percentage-based stop distance cap.
     ATR buffer scales non-linearly with index level. At high ATR, a single
     stop can exceed any reasonable per-trade risk budget. SL_Pct caps the
     maximum stop distance as a percentage of entry price.
     Frozen SL becomes dual-layer: MaxList(ATR_leg, Pct_leg) = tightest.
     SetStopLoss mirrors: MinList(ATR_distance, Pct_distance) = tightest.
     SL_Pct = 0 disables the percentage leg (v14.1 compatible mode).
   BUG-3 FIX: SetStopLoss distance formula unchanged (Close-based proxy).
     Entry via Stop at Box_Btm fills near Close when Close > Box_Btm.
     Close-based distance is a conservative approximation. Combined with
     SL_Pct cap, the engine stop is always a valid safety net.
   FILTER: Opening volatility block (08:45-09:45, Open_Block_End=945).
     Day-session open entries are structurally toxic for consolidation strategies:
     institutions probe/hunt box bottoms at open, invalidating support logic.
     OB930 first pass removed 08:45-09:30 but cascade pushed 19T to 09:45
     (WR 10.5%, -604K). OB945 eliminates cascade; 10:xx is the first
     profitable slot (WR 41%, +134K). Blocks entry SIGNALS whose fills
     would land in the forbidden zone: Time=500 (night session last bar
     -> 09:00 fill) and Time 900..930 (-> 09:15..09:45 fills).
   FILTER: Minimum R:R gate (Min_RR=1.0, requires SL_Pct > 0).
     Rejects entries where Box_Range < Min_RR * Box_Bottom * SL_Pct/100.
     27% of CL_TP trades had R:R < 1.0 (reward < risk). Box width varies
     36-1188 pts but SL_Pct cap is nearly fixed, so narrow boxes create
     structurally negative expected value entries. Optimizable parameter.

 PERFORMANCE (V15.0 w/ OB945, MC9 2026/07/25, 2-lot 2M capital, 1000 slip):
   Net Profit    : 2,446,000 TWD
   Profit Factor : 1.255
   Max Drawdown  : -810,800 (29.4%)
   Win Rate      : 46.3%
   Total Trades  : 376
   Day PF 1.03 / Night PF 1.32

 PERFORMANCE (v14.1 OPTIMIZED, MC9 Excel 2026/07/04, Initial Capital 1M):
   Net Profit    : 2,048,000 TWD (+194% vs v13.4)
   Profit Factor : 1.470 (+24% vs v13.4 1.187)
   Win Rate      : 56.0%
   Reward Ratio  : 1.154
   MDD           : -378,600 (-22.3%)
   Net/MDD       : 5.41
   Total Trades  : 332
   Annual Return : 33.3%
   Sharpe        : 0.302
   Backtest      : 2020/05/12 - 2026/07/04

 OPTIMIZATION (2026-07-04, 2-round MC9 sweep):
   Round 1: range 0.15-0.50 / 1.5-6.0 / 16-64 -> all hit upper bound
   Round 2: expanded 0.15-0.70 / 1.5-10.0 / 16-128 -> converged interior
   Entry_Zone_Pct : 0.30 -> 0.50 (71% of range, plateau confirmed)
   Min_Box_ATR    : 3.0  -> 8.5  (85% of range, off boundary)
   Swing_Lookback : 32   -> 80   (63% of range, plateau confirmed)
================================================================================}

inputs:
    { --- Data2 (60M) Box Detection --- }
    Lookback_Bars(16),
    Range_Shrink_Rate(0.1),
    MA_Len(12),

    { --- V14 Matrix Dimensions --- }
    Entry_Zone_Pct(0.50),       { support zone = bottom 50% of box range (optimized from 0.30) }
    Min_Box_ATR(8.5),           { skip boxes smaller than N * 15M ATR (optimized from 3.0) }
    Swing_Lookback(80),         { 15M bars for dynamic swing high target (optimized from 32) }

    { --- Risk Management (15M) --- }
    ATR_Length(9),
    ATR_Stop_Mult(3.0),
    SL_Pct(0.55),               { V15: percentage stop cap. 0 = disabled. E.g. 0.55 = 0.55% of entry }
    Open_Block_End(945),        { V15: block entries filling before this MC time. 0 = disabled }
    Min_RR(1.0),                { V15: min reward/risk for entry. 0 = disabled. Optimizable }

    { --- Data3 (Daily) Filter Settings --- }
    Daily_MA_Fast(20),
    Daily_MA_Slow(60),

    { --- Holiday Flat Rule v3 (Iron Rule 2026-06-12) --- }
    Holiday_Flat_Time(415),
    Registry_Valid_Until(1270101),
    Manual_Kill_Switch(false),

    { --- Monthly Settlement Flat (2026-06-17) --- }
    Settlement_Flat_Time(1230),

    { --- Frozen SL (v13.2, always-on in v14) --- }
    Freeze_SL_On(true),

    { --- BE layer (DISABLED for range strategies, kept for compat) --- }
    BE_Trigger_Pts(0),
    BE_Offset_Pts(5);

variables:
    { --- Data2 (60M) Box State --- }
    v_Ref_High(0),
    v_Ref_Low(0),
    v_Curr_Range(0),
    v_Ref_Range(0),
    v_is_in_consolidation(false),
    v_Box_Top(0),
    v_Box_Btm(0),

    { --- V14 Matrix State --- }
    v_Mid_Line(0),
    v_Box_Range(0),
    v_Box_Qualified(false),
    v_Support_Zone(0),
    v_Swing_High(0),

    { --- Data2 Trend Filter --- }
    v_60M_MA(0),
    v_Trend_Dir(0),

    { --- Data3 Daily Filter --- }
    v_Daily_MA_Fast(0),
    v_Daily_MA_Slow(0),
    v_Daily_Filter(false),

    { --- Data1 (15M) Execution --- }
    v_Current_ATR(0),
    v_ATR_Buffer(0),
    v_SL_Distance(0),          { V15: SetStopLoss distance (engine level) }
    v_Opening_Block(false),    { V15: true during day-session opening no-trade window }
    v_RR_Qualified(true),      { V15: true when box R:R meets Min_RR threshold }

    { --- Holiday / Settlement --- }
    v_Holiday_Block(false),
    v_Registry_Expired(false),
    Registry_Warn_ID(-1),
    hidx(0),
    v_Settlement_Day(false),

    { --- Frozen SL / Target --- }
    v_SL_Locked(false),
    v_Frozen_SL(0),
    v_Frozen_Target(0),
    v_Work_SL(0),
    v_Work_Target(0),
    v_SL_Pct_Floor(0),        { V15: percentage leg SL price }
    v_BE_Armed(false),
    v_BE_IsFloor(false),

    { --- v15.1 re-entry LABELLING. No behaviour, no new input. --- }
    v_Prev_MP(0),                  { CLAUDE.md Rule #8, set on the last line }
    v_Last_EntryPrice(0),          { EntryPrice is unusable once flat }
    v_Episode_ID(0),               { +1 on each consolidation false->true }
    v_MktExit_Ordered(false),      { a market exit was ordered this bar }
    v_ReEntry_Armed(false),
    v_ReEntry_Price(0),            { the interrupted trade's entry price }
    v_ReEntry_Episode(0);          { the episode it belonged to }

arrays:
    Holiday_Tail[80](0);

{ ==========================================
  0. Holiday Tail Registry (TAIFEX-verified, shared with L1/L2)
  ========================================== }

if CurrentBar = 1 then begin
    Holiday_Tail[1]  = 1190913;  Holiday_Tail[2]  = 1191010;
    Holiday_Tail[3]  = 1200101;
    { 2020 } Holiday_Tail[4]  = 1200121;  Holiday_Tail[5]  = 1200228;
    Holiday_Tail[6]  = 1200402;  Holiday_Tail[7]  = 1200501;
    Holiday_Tail[8]  = 1200625;  Holiday_Tail[9]  = 1201001;
    Holiday_Tail[10] = 1201009;  Holiday_Tail[11] = 1210101;
    { 2021 } Holiday_Tail[12] = 1210206;  Holiday_Tail[13] = 1210227;
    Holiday_Tail[14] = 1210402;  Holiday_Tail[15] = 1210612;
    Holiday_Tail[16] = 1210918;  Holiday_Tail[17] = 1211009;
    Holiday_Tail[18] = 1211231;
    { 2022 } Holiday_Tail[19] = 1220127;  Holiday_Tail[20] = 1220226;
    Holiday_Tail[21] = 1220402;  Holiday_Tail[22] = 1220430;
    Holiday_Tail[23] = 1220603;  Holiday_Tail[24] = 1220909;
    Holiday_Tail[25] = 1221008;  Holiday_Tail[26] = 1221231;
    { 2023 } Holiday_Tail[27] = 1230118;  Holiday_Tail[28] = 1230225;
    Holiday_Tail[29] = 1230401;  Holiday_Tail[30] = 1230429;
    Holiday_Tail[31] = 1230622;  Holiday_Tail[32] = 1230929;
    Holiday_Tail[33] = 1231007;  Holiday_Tail[34] = 1231230;
    { 2024 } Holiday_Tail[35] = 1240206;  Holiday_Tail[36] = 1240228;
    Holiday_Tail[37] = 1240404;  Holiday_Tail[38] = 1240501;
    Holiday_Tail[39] = 1240608;  Holiday_Tail[40] = 1240917;
    Holiday_Tail[41] = 1241010;  Holiday_Tail[42] = 1250101;
    { 2025 } Holiday_Tail[43] = 1250123;  Holiday_Tail[44] = 1250228;
    Holiday_Tail[45] = 1250403;  Holiday_Tail[46] = 1250501;
    Holiday_Tail[47] = 1250530;  Holiday_Tail[48] = 1250927;
    Holiday_Tail[49] = 1251004;  Holiday_Tail[50] = 1251010;
    Holiday_Tail[51] = 1251024;  Holiday_Tail[52] = 1251225;
    Holiday_Tail[53] = 1260101;
    { 2026 (verified: TAIFEX official 115-yr calendar) }
    Holiday_Tail[54] = 1260212;  Holiday_Tail[55] = 1260227;
    Holiday_Tail[56] = 1260403;  Holiday_Tail[57] = 1260501;
    Holiday_Tail[58] = 1260619;  Holiday_Tail[59] = 1260925;
    Holiday_Tail[60] = 1261009;  Holiday_Tail[61] = 1261024;
    Holiday_Tail[62] = 1261225;  Holiday_Tail[63] = 1270101;
end;

v_Holiday_Block = false;

if Time <= 500 then begin
    for hidx = 1 to 80 begin
        if Date = Holiday_Tail[hidx] then
            v_Holiday_Block = true;
    end;
end;

v_Registry_Expired = false;

if Date > Registry_Valid_Until then begin
    v_Registry_Expired = true;
    v_Holiday_Block    = true;
end;

v_Settlement_Day = (DayOfWeek(Date) = 3) and
                   (DayOfMonth(Date) >= 15) and
                   (DayOfMonth(Date) <= 21);

if LastBarOnChart and
   DateToJulian(Date) >= DateToJulian(Registry_Valid_Until) - 30 then begin
    if Registry_Warn_ID < 0 then begin
        Registry_Warn_ID = Text_New(Date, Time, High + 400,
            "HOLIDAY REGISTRY EXPIRES " +
            NumToStr(Registry_Valid_Until, 0) +
            " - REBUILD FROM TAIFEX CALENDAR");
        Text_SetColor(Registry_Warn_ID, Red);
        Text_SetSize(Registry_Warn_ID, 14);
        Text_SetAttribute(Registry_Warn_ID, 1, true);
    end;
end;

{ ==========================================
  1. Commander Logic (Data2 - 60M Box Detection)
  ========================================== }

v_Ref_High   = Highest(High, Lookback_Bars)[1] of Data2;
v_Ref_Low    = Lowest(Low,   Lookback_Bars)[1] of Data2;
v_Curr_Range = (High of Data2) - (Low of Data2);
v_Ref_Range  = v_Ref_High - v_Ref_Low;

v_60M_MA = Average(Close, MA_Len) of Data2;

if Close of Data2 > v_60M_MA then
    v_Trend_Dir = 1
else
    v_Trend_Dir = -1;

if (High of Data2 <= v_Ref_High) and (Low of Data2 >= v_Ref_Low) then begin
    if v_Ref_Range > 0 and (v_Curr_Range / v_Ref_Range <= Range_Shrink_Rate) then begin
        v_is_in_consolidation = true;
        v_Box_Top = v_Ref_High;
        v_Box_Btm = v_Ref_Low;
    end;
end;

if v_is_in_consolidation then begin
    if (Close of Data2 > v_Box_Top) or (Close of Data2 < v_Box_Btm) then
        v_is_in_consolidation = false;
end;

{ v15.1: episode counter. v_is_in_consolidation is sticky, so a false->true
  transition is exactly one new box episode. "Same episode" then costs one
  integer comparison and no parameter at all. }
if v_is_in_consolidation and (v_is_in_consolidation[1] = false) then
    v_Episode_ID = v_Episode_ID + 1;

{ v15.1: reset the market-exit flag ONLY while in position, so on the bar
  the position goes flat it still carries the last in-position value --
  the same idiom L4 relies on with ExitFired. }
if MarketPosition = 1 then
    v_MktExit_Ordered = false;

{ ==========================================
  1b. v15.1 Re-entry state (LABEL ONLY)
  ==========================================
  Capture runs while long; the latch runs on the bar the position goes
  flat, and both sit before the entry section so v_Last_EntryPrice and
  v_MktExit_Ordered still hold their last in-position values. }

if MarketPosition = 1 then
    v_Last_EntryPrice = EntryPrice;

if (v_Prev_MP = 1) and (MarketPosition = 0) then begin
    v_ReEntry_Armed   = (PositionProfit(1) <= 0) and
                        (v_MktExit_Ordered = false);
    v_ReEntry_Price   = v_Last_EntryPrice;
    v_ReEntry_Episode = v_Episode_ID;
end;

{ Disarm when the box episode ends. This is the ONLY disarm, and it is
  structural rather than price based -- L4 v18 fired zero times because its
  price disarm was implied by its own stop, and that trap is avoided here
  by not testing a price at all. }
if (v_ReEntry_Armed = true) and (v_Episode_ID <> v_ReEntry_Episode) then begin
    v_ReEntry_Armed = false;
    v_ReEntry_Price = 0;
end;

{ ==========================================
  2. V14 Box Qualification Matrix (Dim 1)
  ========================================== }

v_Current_ATR = AvgTrueRange(ATR_Length);

v_Box_Range    = 0;
v_Box_Qualified = false;
v_Mid_Line     = 0;
v_Support_Zone = 0;
v_ATR_Buffer   = ATR_Stop_Mult * v_Current_ATR;

if v_is_in_consolidation and v_Box_Top > v_Box_Btm then begin
    v_Box_Range = v_Box_Top - v_Box_Btm;
    v_Mid_Line  = (v_Box_Top + v_Box_Btm) / 2;

    if v_Current_ATR > 0 and (v_Box_Range / v_Current_ATR >= Min_Box_ATR) then
        v_Box_Qualified = true;

    v_Support_Zone = v_Box_Btm + v_Box_Range * Entry_Zone_Pct;
end;

{ ==========================================
  3. Data3 Filter Logic (Daily)
  ========================================== }

v_Daily_MA_Fast = Average(Close, Daily_MA_Fast) of Data3;
v_Daily_MA_Slow = Average(Close, Daily_MA_Slow) of Data3;

if (Close of Data3 > v_Daily_MA_Fast) or
   (Close of Data3 > v_Daily_MA_Slow) then
    v_Daily_Filter = true
else
    v_Daily_Filter = false;

{ ==========================================
  4. Execution Block (requires active box, NOT box qualification)
  Entry is gated by v_Box_Qualified; exit only needs active box.
  BreakExit fires ONLY on true box break (not ATR-ratio drift).
  ========================================== }

if v_is_in_consolidation and v_Box_Top > v_Box_Btm then begin

    { P3b Immediate Stop Guard (Rule #12)
      V15: SetStopContract makes amount per-CONTRACT (lot-invariant).
      V15: SL_Pct caps the engine stop distance as percentage of Close.
      MinList of distances = tightest stop (same logic as L1 V3.1). }
    SetStopContract;
    if v_Box_Qualified and MarketPosition <= 0 then begin
        v_SL_Distance = AbsValue(Close - (v_Box_Btm - v_ATR_Buffer));
        if SL_Pct > 0 then
            v_SL_Distance = MinList(v_SL_Distance, Close * SL_Pct / 100);
        SetStopLoss(v_SL_Distance * BigPointValue);
    end;

    { --- V15 Opening Volatility Filter --- }
    v_Opening_Block = false;
    if Open_Block_End > 0 then begin
        if Time = 500 then v_Opening_Block = true;
        if Time >= 900 and Time < Open_Block_End then v_Opening_Block = true;
    end;

    { --- V15 Reward/Risk Qualification --- }
    v_RR_Qualified = true;
    if Min_RR > 0 and SL_Pct > 0 and v_Box_Range > 0 then begin
        if v_Box_Range < Min_RR * v_Box_Btm * SL_Pct / 100 then
            v_RR_Qualified = false;
    end;

    { --- V14 Entry (Dim 2: Unified Support Zone) --- }
    if v_Box_Qualified and MarketPosition = 0 then begin
        if (v_Trend_Dir = 1) and
           (v_Daily_Filter = true) and
           (v_Holiday_Block = false) and
           (v_Settlement_Day = false) and
           (v_Opening_Block = false) and
           (v_RR_Qualified = true) then begin

            { v15.1 label routing. The two conditions above and the order
              itself are UNTOUCHED -- same price, same order type, same
              bar. Only the label string differs, so the anchor must
              reproduce every metric exactly. }
            if (Close < v_Support_Zone) and
               (Close > v_Box_Btm - v_ATR_Buffer) then begin

                if (v_ReEntry_Armed   = true) and
                   (v_ReEntry_Price   > 0) and
                   (v_Episode_ID      = v_ReEntry_Episode) and
                   (v_Box_Btm        <= v_ReEntry_Price) then
                    Buy ("CL_ReEntry") next bar at v_Box_Btm Stop
                else
                    Buy ("CL_Entry")   next bar at v_Box_Btm Stop;

            end;

        end;
    end;

    { --- V14 Exit (Dim 3: Dynamic Target) --- }
    if MarketPosition = 1 then begin

        if Freeze_SL_On = true then begin
            if v_SL_Locked = false then begin
                v_Frozen_SL = v_Box_Btm - v_ATR_Buffer;

                { V15: SL_Pct percentage leg (dual-layer frozen SL).
                  MaxList picks the highest price = tightest for long. }
                if SL_Pct > 0 then begin
                    v_SL_Pct_Floor = EntryPrice - (EntryPrice * SL_Pct / 100);
                    v_Frozen_SL = MaxList(v_Frozen_SL, v_SL_Pct_Floor);
                end;

                v_Swing_High = Highest(High, Swing_Lookback);
                v_Frozen_Target = MinList(v_Swing_High, v_Box_Top);
                if v_Frozen_Target < v_Mid_Line + v_Current_ATR then
                    v_Frozen_Target = v_Box_Top;

                v_SL_Locked = true;
            end;

            v_Work_SL     = v_Frozen_SL;
            v_Work_Target = v_Frozen_Target;

        end else begin
            v_Work_SL     = v_Box_Btm - v_ATR_Buffer;

            { V15: SL_Pct percentage leg (non-frozen path) }
            if SL_Pct > 0 then begin
                v_SL_Pct_Floor = EntryPrice - (EntryPrice * SL_Pct / 100);
                v_Work_SL = MaxList(v_Work_SL, v_SL_Pct_Floor);
            end;

            v_Swing_High  = Highest(High, Swing_Lookback);
            v_Work_Target = MinList(v_Swing_High, v_Box_Top);
            if v_Work_Target < v_Mid_Line + v_Current_ATR then
                v_Work_Target = v_Box_Top;
        end;

        { BE layer (disabled by default, kept for compat) }
        v_BE_IsFloor = false;
        if BE_Trigger_Pts > 0 then begin
            if (Close - EntryPrice) >= BE_Trigger_Pts then
                v_BE_Armed = true;
            if v_BE_Armed and
               (EntryPrice + BE_Offset_Pts > v_Work_SL) then begin
                v_Work_SL    = EntryPrice + BE_Offset_Pts;
                v_BE_IsFloor = true;
            end;
        end;

        { Exit orders }
        Sell ("CL_TP") next bar at v_Work_Target Limit;

        if v_BE_IsFloor then
            Sell ("CL_BE") next bar at v_Work_SL Stop
        else
            Sell ("CL_SL") next bar at v_Work_SL Stop;

    end;

end else begin
    { ==========================================
      5. True Box Break Exit (consolidation ended)
      ========================================== }
    if MarketPosition = 1 then begin
        Sell ("CL_BreakExit") next bar at Market;
        v_MktExit_Ordered = true;
    end;
end;

{ ==========================================
  6. Safety Exits (Priority 0, always active)
  ========================================== }

if MarketPosition = 1 then begin

    if v_Registry_Expired then begin
        Sell ("CL_RegistryEnd") next bar at Market;
        v_MktExit_Ordered = true;
    end
    else if v_Holiday_Block and Time >= Holiday_Flat_Time then begin
        Sell ("CL_Holiday") next bar at Market;
        v_MktExit_Ordered = true;
    end
    else if v_Settlement_Day and Time >= Settlement_Flat_Time then begin
        Sell ("CL_Settlement") next bar at Market;
        v_MktExit_Ordered = true;
    end;

    if Manual_Kill_Switch then begin
        Sell ("CL_Kill") next bar at Market;
        v_MktExit_Ordered = true;
    end;

end;

{ ==========================================
  7. State Reset (flat)
  ========================================== }

if MarketPosition = 0 then begin
    v_SL_Locked     = false;
    v_Frozen_SL     = 0;
    v_Frozen_Target = 0;
    v_SL_Pct_Floor  = 0;
    v_BE_Armed      = false;
    v_BE_IsFloor    = false;
end;

{ CLAUDE.md Rule #8: v_Prev_MP is updated on the LAST line, so every block
  above reads the PREVIOUS bar's position. The re-entry latch depends on it. }
v_Prev_MP = MarketPosition;
